# Run from the repo root:  python3 test/mutation/mutate.py test/mutation/mutants.py -- npx vitest run
# (the driver checks the suite is green first; do not edit the tree while it runs; each pattern must occur exactly once)
#
# Not listed, because they cannot change behaviour:
#  - dropping the `typeof value !== "number"` half of the check in formatMonthlyCost: Number.isFinite is already false for every
#    non-number, so only the type narrowing (which tsc enforces) depends on it;
#  - looking for the cheapest paid row among all rows instead of the main chart's: the row at the 90th percentile is always in the main
#    chart (it costs less than three times itself), so whenever any row is paid, the cheapest one is too.

